ral.png","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/02_Lisburn_Cathedral.png/500px-02_Lisburn_Cathedral.png","caption":"Lisburn Cathedral","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:02_Lisburn_Cathedral.png","ok_print":false},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Kilwarlin_church.jpg/960px-Kilwarlin_church.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Kilwarlin_church.jpg/500px-Kilwarlin_church.jpg","caption":"Kilwarlin Moravian Church","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kilwarlin_church.jpg","ok_print":false}],"intro":{"body":"Lisburn is a market town traditionally in County Antrim north of the River Lagan; a small part lies south of the river in County Down. The counties of Northern Ireland are no longer units of governance so since 2015 it's been within the \"super-district\" of Lisburn and Castlereagh. It's best known as the seat of linen manufacture in Ireland, but it's also notorious as the site of the former Long Kesh or Maze prison. With a population of 51,400 in 2021, Lisburn was officially dubbed a \"city\" in 2002 but this is just ceremonial. Not only does it continue to feel like a town, but \"city\" hereabouts means the metropolis of Belfast 9 miles north; so a town is how it's described on this page.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Lisburn","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Lisburn","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Lisburn is a cathedral city in the United Kingdom with a good spread of museums and gardens. St Peter's Cathedral and the Ulster Museum lead the sights, with Hillsborough Castle close by; seven hours covers the main list, June through August.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":77506,"visit_h":6.8}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-hillsborough-castle","name":"Hillsborough Castle","kind":"Castle","lat":54.46138,"lon":-6.08604,"dist_km":7.6,"sig":1.306,"rank_score":8.98,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Castle in Northern Irela